Algorithm:

1. Start the program.
2. Accept the number of users.
3. Create an adjacency list to represent the graph.
4. Accept the number of friendship pairs.
5. For each friendship pair, accept two user IDs, u and v.
6. Add v to the adjacency list of u and u to the adjacency list of v, because friendships are undirected.
7. Display the list of friends for every user.
8. Accept the user ID whose friends are to be checked.
9. If the selected user ID is valid, display all directly connected friends; otherwise, display an invalid user message.
10. Stop the program.
